<?nvs
// The operator's error-handler script — ADR 0020 § 1's rung above every
// `catch`. `nvs.toml` names this file for `examples/logging/throws.nvs`,
// and the engine runs it after that program has stopped, out of a budget
// reserved for exactly this so that a script which died at its memory
// ceiling still has enough left to say so.
//
// It prints one line because that is all a handler owes: evidence it ran.
// Anything it wants to know about the failure arrives through
// `Core\Fatal`, whose `onUncaughtThrow` receives the real `Throwable`
// rather than a rendering of it.
echo 'handler ran', "\n";
